 tv show  and it fits right in on a premium cable  channel and yet for a brief period  it actually ran on a broadcast network  in 2007  and 2008 the writers guild of america  went on strike for more than three  months  with more than 60 scripted television  series shutting down production  as a result of the strike the big  networks were left with major holes in  their tv schedules  with relatively tame crime and cop shows  like csi and criminal minds benched  cbs pulled content from its corporate  sibling showtime  all 12 episodes from the first season of  dexter aired in a carefully edited form  which reportedly marked the first time  in tv history that a broadcast channel  aired a whole season of a premium cable  series  two people in the cast of dexter found  love amidst the show's dark premise  michael c hall and jennifer carpenter  who played dexter's adoptive sister  deborah morgan  the general public didn't even know the  two have been a couple for more than a  year and a half until they showed up at  the golden globes in january 2009  having eloped and gotten married just a  few days prior  but the marriage wasn't meant to last  just about three years later  paul and carpenter released a statement  to entertainment weekly  announcing that they had separated and  were filing for divorce  it was evidently an amicable enough  split that hall and carpenter continued  to work with each other on dexter for a  few more years  still art managed to imitate life when  dexter writers explored a romantic  relationship  between the brother and sister awkward  well probably but the actors handled it  like prose  over the course of 96 episodes dexter  morgan killed a lot of people  but how many lives did the character  take in total the authors of the  dexter's kill list page on a dexter fan  site  carefully watched all episodes and tally  the number of victims  by both counting up who he killed on  screen and looking at the number of  blood slides he kept in his box of  