ld have done if he'd  been in charge of crafting the show's  final scene  he said in the very last scene of the  series dexter wakes up  dexter's opening his eyes and he's on  the execution table at the florida  penitentiary  they're just starting to administer the  drugs and he looks out through the  window to the observation gallery and in  the gallery are all the people that  dexter killed as phillips conceived it  the observers would have been everyone  who ever died as a result of dexter's  actions  from the trinity killer to laguardia and  doakes to his minor kills of the week  a lot of people didn't like the way  dexter wrapped up no matter how you feel  about it  it's hard to argue that this would have  been one hell of a way to go  the silver lining of keeping dexter  alive was always that the show could one  day see a revival  and get a second chance to wrap things  up in a satisfying way  now that do-over is finally coming to  pass in 2020 seven years after dexter  aired his last episode  showtime ordered 10 new episodes to be  presented as a limited series  michael c hall signed on to once again  play dexter while the series original  executive producer clyde phillips  agreed to serve a showrunner in april  2021  showtime unveiled a teaser trailer for  the revival and announced that it would  air the following fall  plot details have initially been scarce  but reports indicate that the episodes  will find dexter morgan hiding out under  the assumed identity of jim lindsey  in the small town of iron lake new york  there a mystery will ensnare the mayor  the chief of police  and the true crime podcast host as well  as dexter morgan  back from the dead to kill again  dexter's dark passengers still with him  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one  you

